# Response headers for Cloudflare Pages (other hosts serve this as a plain file and ignore it).

# Code and styles: browsers and Cloudflare check with the site before reusing a copy (an unchanged
# file costs only a "not modified" reply). They were kept a year, as their names change whenever
# they do, but then a bad copy stuck: during a deploy, a request for a new file can reach the old
# version of the site, which answers with the game's page. Cloudflare kept that page as the game's
# code, and Chrome showed a blank page for hours (2026-10-22, DESIGN.md).
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# Every response.
#  - nosniff: files are only ever what their type says.
#  - The referrer: other sites see only "strokes.fun", never a page's address.
#  - No camera, microphone, location, payment or USB access.
#  - No other site may show the game in a frame (X-Frame-Options, and frame-ancestors below).
#  - The content security policy: only the site's own scripts, data and images (plus data: and
#    blob: images, for the share card), and Cloudflare Web Analytics: the script Cloudflare adds to
#    the page (static.cloudflareinsights.com), reporting to strokes.fun/cdn-cgi/rum or
#    cloudflareinsights.com. It ran report-only on the first publish, and nothing was reported. A
#    page or script it doesn't allow is blocked, and shows in the browser's console.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; connect-src 'self' https://cloudflareinsights.com; font-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
